<% content_for :meta_title, "Terms of Service | Red Tape LA" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "Terms of use for Red Tape LA. Understand how we operate and what we can and can't do." %>

<div class="hero-about">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">
      How Red Tape LA works and what to expect
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container-narrow">

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">What Red Tape LA Is</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      Red Tape LA is a volunteer-run project documenting bureaucratic barriers in LA's housing development process. We collect real experiences, identify patterns, and use aggregated data to advocate for systemic reform.
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      We're an independent project. We're not affiliated with the City of LA, any city department, or any government agency.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">What We Can Do</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      <strong>We can:</strong>
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      • Document your experience with LA's building bureaucracy<br>
      • Analyze stories to find patterns<br>
      • Share anonymized data with policymakers, journalists, and advocacy organizations<br>
      • Publish reports on systemic issues<br>
      • Make your story count toward fixing the system
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">What We Can't Do</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      <strong>We cannot:</strong>
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      • Expedite your permits or inspections<br>
      • Intervene in your individual case<br>
      • Provide legal advice<br>
      • Guarantee any specific outcomes<br>
      • Act as a liaison with city departments<br>
      • Resolve your individual bureaucratic problems
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      If you need legal help, consult an attorney. If you need help navigating city processes, consider contacting your City Council representative or a housing advocacy organization.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Your Responsibilities</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      When you share a story with Red Tape LA, you agree to:
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      • Provide accurate information to the best of your knowledge<br>
      • Not submit false, misleading, or defamatory content<br>
      • Not include personal information about others without their consent<br>
      • Understand that we may edit your story for clarity or length<br>
      • Understand that we use anonymized data for advocacy purposes
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">How We Use Your Story</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      When you submit a story, you grant Red Tape LA permission to:
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      • Review and verify your submission<br>
      • Include your story in our database for analysis<br>
      • Share anonymized, aggregated data with policymakers, journalists, and advocates<br>
      • Publish your story on our Public Stories page (if you opted in)<br>
      • Reference your story in reports and advocacy materials (always anonymized)
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      We will never share your name, email address, or other identifying information publicly or with officials.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">No Warranties</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      Red Tape LA is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. We make no guarantees about:
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      • The accuracy or completeness of information on this site<br>
      • The effectiveness of our advocacy efforts<br>
      • Specific policy changes or outcomes<br>
      • The site's availability or uptime
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Red Tape LA and its volunteers are not liable for any damages arising from:
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      • Your use of this website<br>
      • Your reliance on information provided<br>
      • Your participation in this project<br>
      • Any delays, errors, or omissions in our service
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Content Moderation</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      We reserve the right to:
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      • Review all submissions before publication<br>
      • Decline to publish stories that don't meet our standards<br>
      • Remove content that violates these terms<br>
      • Edit submissions for clarity, length, or to remove identifying information
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Termination</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      We reserve the right to suspend or terminate access to Red Tape LA for anyone who violates these terms or engages in abusive behavior.
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      You can request deletion of your story and data at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:john@redtape.la">john@redtape.la</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Changes to These Terms</h2>
    <p class="text-large">
      We may update these terms from time to time. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes acceptance of the new terms.
    </p>
    <p class="text-large">
      Last updated: <%= Date.today.strftime("%B %d, %Y") %>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-large mb-0">
      Questions about these terms? Email us at <a href="mailto:john@redtape.la">john@redtape.la</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

</div>
